'''Pere Bosch''' (born 1971) is a [[Volisania|Volisanian]] corporate executive and the CEO of [[Abyala Telecom]], the largest telecommunications provider in southern [[Abyala]] and [[Potocsí]]. He is the cousin of Balboan musician [[Març Bosch i Guzmán]].

== Career ==

Bosch began his career in 1993 as a salesman at TeleVoli, then a mid-sized telecom provider in [[Volisania]]. Over the following two decades, he rose through the company's commercial and operations divisions, eventually becoming CEO in 2008. Under his leadership, TeleVoli grew to become the second-largest telecommunications provider in Volisania, expanding its mobile and broadband customer base through aggressive pricing and network modernisation.

In 2023, Bosch was recruited as CEO of [[Abyala Telecom]] by chairman [[Jordi Arimany i Soler]], succeeding the company's previous leadership. His appointment was seen as a signal of AT's ambition to bring in outside expertise from a mature, competitive telecom market to drive its next phase of growth across its six markets.

== Personal life ==

Bosch is 55 years old and lives in [[Sant Cristòfor]], [[Balboa]]. He is married and has two children. He is the cousin of [[Març Bosch i Guzmán]], a Balboan musician.

